:"Q05321","text":"Onyx GF is a chopped-glass-fiber-filled nylon filament built for industrial tooling and end-use parts.","source":"R-MARKFORGED-Onyx-GF-Material-Datasheet","at":"p. 1: HIGH-STRENGTH COLOR COMPOSITE, first sentence","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement","conditions":"Maker intended-use claim. Printed-property specimens in this sheet use an FX10; continuous-fiber reinforcement is separate and not transferred to ordinary H2C printed parts."},{"id":"Q07978","text":"Compatible with Continuous Fiber Reinforcement, Onyx GF can be reinforced for higher-load applications where structural performance is critical.","source":"R-MARKFORGED-Onyx-GF-Material-Datasheet","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07980","text":"Select colors support safety compliance and error-proofing workflows where color-coded, identifiable tooling is an operational requirement.","source":"R-MARKFORGED-Onyx-GF-Material-Datasheet","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07981","text":"Designed for automotive, aerospace, defense, and other demanding manufacturing environments, Onyx GF is built for teams that require both material performance and visual organization at scale.","source":"R-MARKFORGED-Onyx-GF-Material-Datasheet","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Benefits","items":[{"id":"Q07977","text":"It delivers the surface finish, dimensional accuracy, and print reliability of Onyx with added functional color and non-conductive properties.","source":"R-MARKFORGED-Onyx-GF-Material-Datasheet","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Pitfalls and limitations","items":[{"id":"Q07982","text":"The mechanical and thermal properties of Onyx GF may vary with print orientation.","source":"R-MARKFORGED-Onyx-GF-Material-Datasheet","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Surface finish","items":[{"id":"Q07979","text":"Available in six colors, Onyx GF brings visual differentiation to the factory floor without added process steps.","source":"R-MARKFORGED-Onyx-GF-Material-Datasheet","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Adhesion between layers","items":[{"id":"Q07983","text":"In tension, most parts are strongest when the print orientation and loading direction are parallel, and weakest when the print orientation and loading direction are perpendicular.","source":"R-MARKFORGED-Onyx-GF-Material-Datasheet","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Moisture sensitivity","items":[{"id":"Q07984","text":"The mechanical properties of Onyx GF may change based on the moisture absorbed from its ambient environment.","source":"R-MARKFORGED-Onyx-GF-Material-Datasheet","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07985","text":"Increased moisture content will result in a more durable part, behavior that is typical of nylon-based materials.","source":"R-MARKFORGED-Onyx-GF-Material-Datasheet","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]}]},{"id":"G166-02","name":"Eumakers PA Nylon Glass Fiber","maker":"Eumakers","variant":null,"diameter":"1.75 mm","twins":[],"composition":"\"Glass Fiber Reinforced Polyammide\" (the maker's filament data sheet); its safety data sheet says \"Polyamide - additives/modifiers\" and names no polyamide or fibre load","certifications":null,"availability":null,"claim":null,"values":[{"key":"density","id":"V015614","value":1180,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"R-EUMAKERS-INTAKE-20261019-50de915f1dbb","page":2,"twin":null,"at":"Density"},{"key":"tensileModulusXY","id":"V015623","value":2.534,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"R-EUMAKERS-INTAKE-20261019-da9a178eef3e","page":3,"twin":null,"admitted":["moisture","treatment"],